From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] session: hold the backend weakly for log callbacks

backendInUse, which only routes libseat and libinput log messages to the
backend's logger, held a strong reference that nothing released. The
backend therefore outlived the compositor's own reset and was destroyed by
libaquamarine's static destructors at process exit. By then other
libraries' destructors may have run: with NVIDIA's EGL driver (libEGL_nvidia
unloads libnvidia-eglcore in its destructor), freeing the outputs' GBM
buffers calls into unloaded code and the compositor crashes on every exit.

Hold it weakly, so the backend is destroyed when its owner drops it, while
the renderer is still alive. The log callbacks already return early when it
is unset.

Tested on a Jetson Nano (Tegra210) with Hyprland on Mesa Zink over NVIDIA's
L4T R36 Vulkan driver: no crash when the session ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018sL3QMUPGLPrQaT1qEGWwE
---
--- a/src/backend/Session.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/Session.cpp
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 // we can't really do better with libseat/libinput logs
 // because they don't allow us to pass "data" or anything...
 // Nobody should create multiple backends anyways really
-Hyprutils::Memory::CSharedPointer<CBackend> backendInUse;
+Hyprutils::Memory::CWeakPointer<CBackend> backendInUse;
 
 //
 static Aquamarine::eBackendLogLevel logLevelFromLibseat(libseat_log_level level) {
